# Supabase — personalized guest groups for /i/[slug]
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values from your Supabase project
# (Project Settings > API). NEVER commit real keys. This example file is safe
# to track; .env* is gitignored except for .env.example.
#
# When BOTH values are present at BUILD time, /i/[slug] reads guest groups from
# the `guest_groups` table (see supabase/migrations/) and renders each request
# against it so is_active soft-deletes and edits are immediate. When either is
# absent, the app falls back to the in-repo mock data (src/lib/guest-groups.ts)
# and the route stays fully static with zero config.
#
# Server-only. Do NOT prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — they must never reach the
# client bundle. The service-role key bypasses RLS, so keep it secret and rotate
# it if it leaks. For a read-only public deployment you can later switch the
# boundary to the anon key plus a SELECT RLS policy.

SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
